        "content": "UniversalVault is a macOS menu-bar app that stores structured personal records encrypted on this Mac. Control+Option+V opens a search palette over whatever app you are in; search a field, press Return, and the value is typed into the focused field. An item can be marked protected, which seals its fields under a second key and asks for Touch ID before they are read; the palette shows a sealed count and unlocks them with Touch ID. Editors autosave and show a Saved badge. An item can be marked for agents, which lets a local command print its non-sensitive fields as JSON. The vault opens at launch without a prompt. Sleep and screen lock seal protected items only; signing out or quitting closes the whole vault. There is no cloud sync.\n\nIt is your first ten minutes with it. Describe what you expected, what you looked for, what you tried, and what the product should have told you at each step. Say where you stopped and why.\n",
